                "text": "**Analyzing Train Examples**\n\nOkay, I'm diving into the train examples. Just starting with the basic structure \u2013 looking at the blocks, their colors, row and column ranges, and deriving the width and height of each. I'm noting the gaps between them, starting with vertical and horizontal distances. This looks like a promising start.\n\n\n**Investigating Block Overlaps**\n\nI'm now focusing on overlaps. Analyzing the column ranges reveals a pattern with the 8s in the output \u2013 they appear at the center columns of the overlaps. For instance, in Example 1, columns 3 and 4 are the center of the overlap of columns 2, 3, 4, and 5. It seems this center column concept applies whether the overlap's length is even (cols 3, 4) or odd (col 5). I am now looking at how this applies across different examples.\n\n\n",
